    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8ce6f95c-75a2-5fc8-8e2f-36326e20b3d6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\\cot\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}{2\\left(1-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\right)}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)=2sc$.\n\n Also, $\\cot\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\right)=\\frac{c}{s}$.\n\nRewrite the quotient ratio and cancel. Use $s^2+c^2=1$, factor the difference of squares, then cancel the matching binomial.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc\\frac{c}{s}}{2(1-s)} &=\\frac{2c^2}{2(1-s)} \\\\ &=\\frac{1-s^2}{(1-s)} \\\\ &=\\frac{(1-s)(1+s)}{(1-s)} \\\\ &=(1+s) \\\\ &=\\left(1+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
